# Known differences between the outline and the reference's parse.
# Each line: the case, the path of the first node that differs, and why.
# A case listed here fails its test once it stops differing, so the line is
# removed when a release of goldmark reads it as the reference does.

# The specification's, extensions' and regression tests' examples.
spec/0610 document/paragraph[0]/text[0] the reference's autolink extension finds an address inside <...> holding a space
spec/0614 document/paragraph[0]/text[0] the reference's autolink extension finds an email address inside <...> that is no autolink
extensions/0018 document/paragraph[5]/text[0] goldmark reads strikethrough of unequal runs of tildes
extensions/0019 document/paragraph[6]/text[0] the reference finds an email address directly after a /
extensions/0023 document/footnote_definition[2]/paragraph[0] goldmark reads a footnote definition's indented first line as a code block
regression/0009 document/paragraph[0] goldmark counts meta among the tags opening an HTML block of the sixth type, which CommonMark does not
regression/0014 document/paragraph[0] goldmark counts meta among the tags opening an HTML block of the sixth type, which CommonMark does not
regression/0017 document/html_block[0] goldmark reads a closing </script> tag alone on a line as a paragraph
regression/0019 document/paragraph[0] goldmark reads a lone | over a delimiter row as a table of one column
regression/0023 document/paragraph[0]/text[0] goldmark reads emphasis inside a footnote label, which the reference reads as text
regression/0024 document/paragraph[0]/text[0] goldmark reads strikethrough inside a footnote label, which the reference reads as text

# Addresses written without < and >, which the reference's autolink
# extension and goldmark's linkify extension find in different places.
archdoc/address-after-bracket document/paragraph[0]/text[0] the reference finds an address after a ], where GFM allows none, and reads the link after it as part of it
archdoc/address-after-paren document/paragraph[0]/text[0] goldmark finds an address after a ), where GFM allows none, and reads the link after it as part of it
archdoc/address-after-punctuation document/paragraph[0]/text[0] the reference finds an address with a scheme after punctuation GFM allows none after
archdoc/address-after-tab document/paragraph[0]/text[0] the reference finds an address after a tab, where goldmark finds none
archdoc/address-after-unclosed-angle document/paragraph[0]/text[0] the reference finds an address after a < that opens no autolink
archdoc/address-after-tag document/paragraph[0]/text[0] goldmark finds an address directly after a tag
archdoc/address-after-backtick document/paragraph[0]/text[0] goldmark finds an address directly after a backtick that opens no code span
archdoc/address-past-backslash document/paragraph[0]/link[0] the reference ends an address past a backslash, where goldmark ends it at the backslash
archdoc/address-ending-in-backslash document/paragraph[0]/link[0] the reference keeps a backslash ending an address in it
archdoc/address-ending-in-delimiters document/paragraph[0]/text[0] goldmark finds an address ending in _ and ~, which the reference finds none in
archdoc/address-www-then-punctuation document/paragraph[0]/link[0] the reference finds www. followed by punctuation as an address
archdoc/email-empty-domain-label document/paragraph[0]/link[0] the reference finds an email address whose domain begins with a .
archdoc/email-followed-by-at document/paragraph[0]/text[0] goldmark finds an email address followed by a second @

# Tables, which goldmark begins and ends on lines where the reference does not.
archdoc/table-after-lone-pipe document/paragraph[0] goldmark reads a lone | over a delimiter row as a table of one column
archdoc/table-in-list-item document/list[0]/item[0]/paragraph[0] goldmark begins a table inside a list item where the reference reads a paragraph
archdoc/table-in-blockquote document/block_quote[0]/paragraph[0] goldmark begins a table inside a blockquote where the reference reads a paragraph
archdoc/table-in-footnote-definition document/footnote_definition[0]/paragraph[0] goldmark begins a table inside a footnote definition where the reference reads a paragraph
archdoc/table-after-definition document the reference reads [1]: over a delimiter row as a table, where goldmark reads a link reference definition whose destination is on the next line
archdoc/table-row-after-list-marker document/table[0] goldmark reads a line holding a list marker alone as a row of the table
archdoc/table-row-indented document/table[0] goldmark reads an indented line after a row as another row

# Raw HTML.
archdoc/lowercase-declaration-block document/paragraph[0]/link[0] goldmark reads <! before a lowercase letter as a declaration opening an HTML block, as CommonMark 0.31.2 does, where GFM 0.29 requires an uppercase letter
archdoc/lowercase-declaration-inline document/paragraph[0]/text[0] goldmark reads <! before a lowercase letter as a declaration within a line, as CommonMark 0.31.2 does, where GFM 0.29 requires an uppercase letter
archdoc/processing-instruction-empty document/paragraph[0]/html_inline[0] goldmark reads <?> as a whole processing instruction, where the reference reads on to the next ?>

